> Retain the original nine-symbol cap sweep

Use the original weights[20,17,6,3,2,2,2,1,1] and caps4,...,8. The original large-cap reference call used L=N=9; the effective cap is now8 because no positive-weight optimum needs deeper than N−1. This reference is the same canonical package-merge producer at an unconstraining cap, not an independent Huffman implementation.

The exact decimal cost column is authoritative. The plotted double values are presentation conversions of those exact costs. Ties can admit several equally optimal length vectors; initial singleton ties follow the native std::sort behavior, so cross-toolchain ID/length tie identity is not promised.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/package_merge_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto weights       = dm::algorithms::package_merge_demo_weights();
  auto unconstrained = dm::algorithms::package_merge_run(weights, int(weights.size()));
  std::vector<double> x, y;
  std::print(
      "Exact unconstrained-cap cost: {}. Requested cap: {}. Effective levels: {}.\n\n",
      dm::algorithms::package_merge_cost_decimal(unconstrained.weighted_cost),
      unconstrained.requested_max_length,
      unconstrained.effective_levels);
  std::print(
      "| requested cap | actual max length | exact weighted cost | actual code lengths | displayed "
      "Kraft sum | exact Kraft equality |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- |\n");
  for (int cap = 4; cap <= 8; ++cap) {
    auto r = dm::algorithms::package_merge_run(weights, cap);
    x.push_back(cap);
    y.push_back(dm::algorithms::package_merge_cost_approximation(r.weighted_cost));
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | {} | `{}` | {:.12f} | {} |\n",
        cap,
        r.actual_max_length,
        dm::algorithms::package_merge_cost_decimal(r.weighted_cost),
        r.lengths,
        double(r.kraft_sum),
        r.kraft_equality);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.lines(x, y, "actual cap cost", dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255})
      .points(x, y, dm::graphics::RGBA{37, 99, 235, 255}, 3.)
      .abline_h(
          dm::algorithms::package_merge_cost_approximation(unconstrained.weighted_cost),
          dm::graphics::RGB{22, 163, 74},
          1.5);
  p.legend({"actual cap cost", "unconstrained"}, {{37, 99, 235}, {22, 163, 74}});
  p.title("Original nine symbols: actual optimal weighted cost")
      .x_label("requested maximum code length")
      .y_label("weighted path cost, display conversion")
      .save_svg("build/package_merge_original.svg");
}
```
