> Feasibility, singletons and full-width costs

All original weights must be positive and the requested cap strictly positive, including empty/singleton inputs. For N≥2 an infeasible2^L<N is rejected before list construction. The two maximum uint64weights in the control table already have a weighted cost above64bits; exact128bit package/cost arithmetic prevents wraparound. If128bits cannot hold a computed cost, the call throws rather than changing cost order.

The default complete symbol cap is1000000 and the cumulative actual working-member-copy cap is10000000; either zero disables its policy. A trace separately pre-admits weights/lengths and limits each actual coin/list/selection copy: root requested/effective controls2, input/output entries2N, each constructed coin1+members, each retained list1+IDs and every final selected ID. Default1000000 logical history units, zero disabling. These are explicit work/output policies rather than allocator, byte or live-memory estimates. No caller data is mutated, no references remain, and no partial trace escapes failure.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/package_merge_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<std::vector<std::uint64_t>> inputs{
      {},
      {7},
      {std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max(), std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max()},
      dm::algorithms::package_merge_demo_weights()};
  std::vector<int>         caps{1, 1, std::numeric_limits<int>::max(), 4};
  std::vector<std::string> labels{"empty", "singleton", "full-width pair", "original feasible"};
  std::vector<double>      levels;
  std::print(
      "| control | requested cap | actual effective levels | exact weighted cost | displayed Kraft "
      "sum | exact equality |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
    auto r = dm::algorithms::package_merge_run(inputs[i], caps[i]);
    levels.push_back(r.effective_levels);
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
        labels[i],
        caps[i],
        r.effective_levels,
        dm::algorithms::package_merge_cost_decimal(r.weighted_cost),
        double(r.kraft_sum),
        r.kraft_equality);
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot(levels, labels, "actual effective levels");
  p.title("Package-merge controls: useful depth and exact costs")
      .x_label("explicit original-weight control")
      .y_label("actual effective levels")
      .save_svg("build/package_merge_controls.svg");
}
```
